# Sync How it works with game rules

When changing **player-facing** fantasy rules — scoring values, season multipliers, finish points, lock/DNQ behavior, salary-cap/roster defaults, money-hole quirks, Harry’s Big Hole, Nickname de Sarge, or similar — update the public guide in the same change.

## Required

1. Update `src/routes/how-it-works.tsx` so copy, tables, and examples match the new rules.
2. Prefer **deriving** displayed numbers from `src/lib/scoring.ts` (`SCORING`, `BONUS_SCORING`, `MONEY_HOLE_MULTIPLIER`, `finishPoints`, `multiplierForEventType`, etc.) or other shared constants — do not hardcode literals that can drift.
3. If the guide needs a constant that doesn’t exist yet, add it to the shared module and import it; don’t duplicate magic numbers in the route.

## Checklist

- [ ] Hole / bonus / finish / multiplier / money-hole numbers in the guide match `src/lib/scoring.ts`
- [ ] Lock, DNQ, roster, and cap wording matches product behavior
- [ ] Named quirks (Harry’s Big Hole, Nickname de Sarge, etc.) still describe current rules

## Out of scope

Internal refactors, UI-only tweaks, or scoring implementation details that do not change what players see — no guide update required.
